;B[dd];W[qq];B[dp];W[qc];B[dj];W[fq];B[dn];W[kp];B[qf];W[nc];B[pj];W[ql]LB[pn:A]
C[Although it allows black to play 13, this move is good. If white plays 12 at 'A', then black can play at 12 with good feeling.]
;B[po];W[op];B[oo];W[np];B[qp];W[rq];B[no];W[mp];B[ok]C[Excellent point. The alternative at 43 leaves white with aji at 31.]
;W[fc];B[id];W[fe];B[df];W[db];B[cc];W[ib];B[fg]LB[dr:B]C[It is not so important to play here in this case. Ikken tobi at 'B' is the largest move.]
;W[qi];B[qj];W[rj];B[qd]C[Very bad aji-keshi, this move serves only to strengthen white.]
;W[pc];B[pi];W[rh];B[qh];W[ri];B[qg];W[qn];B[pm]C[To diconnect white by playing sagari from 17 is also a viable way of playing.]
;W[pl];B[ol];W[ro];B[gp]LB[dr:B]C[It is still better to play at 'B'.];W[fp];B[fo]
;W[go];B[fn]C[It is possible to play at 52 leading to a difficult fight.];W[hp]
;B[gn];W[gq];B[gd];W[fd];B[hg];W[dg];B[cf]C[This is a strong response to white 56. To play at 65 would give white a better chance of making life among the side.]
;W[ff]C[Not good. White has little chance of success with a direct manoeuvre. He should play more lightly around 72.]
;B[gg]C[This move should be at 64, Black's stones at 23 and 53 are not important, and more attention should be paid to securing the centre. ]
;W[cj];B[ck];W[dk];B[bk]LB[cl:C]C[It is more natural to play at 'C'. After the sequence to 69, 'C' would have been a much better placed stone than 63.]
;W[eg];B[ef];W[ej];B[di];W[ei];B[ci];W[hj];B[gi]C[It is better to omit 71, 72 exchange, and simply play at 73.]
